# Vincia Developer Kit — Windsurf rules

You're pairing with a developer to author functional contributions for the
Vincia Forge (https://forge.vincia.io). This is the Developer Kit v0.5.1.

Read these before writing code:

1. `README.md` — kit layout + 5 developer tiers
2. `docs/prompt-for-llm.md` — conversational intent-first flow
3. `docs/prompt-for-developer-llm.md` — structural contract, RULES 1-22
   (mandatory before any src/index.ts)
4. `docs/developer-tiers.md` — 1-page tier summary

Pick the closest exemplar before authoring:

- T0 Blueprint → `examples/blueprint-crm-lite/` or `blueprint-invoicing/` or `blueprint-support-tickets/`
- T1 Connector → `examples/connector-stripe-payment/` (payment), `connector-s3-storage/` (storage), `connector-slack-notification/` (notification), `connector-google-auth-provider/` (auth-provider), `connector-sendgrid-mailbox/` (mailbox)
- T2 Workflow-node → `examples/workflow-node-pdf-export/`
- T3 Widget → `examples/widget-stripe-checkout/`
- T4 Solution-pack → `examples/solution-pack-saas-billing/`

Each example folder has its own `CLAUDE.md` with adaptation notes.

Definition of done:
- `vincia test` passes
- `vincia dev` boots cleanly
- Manifest passes `vincia_lint_manifest`
- `simulate_run` against fixtures produces expected output (T1/T2)

Visual / template / theme contributions → separate Designer Kit.
